onsible for the production of immune-related cytokines and chemokines. This cell type secretes glycoproteins and hyaluronic acid, has abundant granular endoplasmic reticulum, but contains fewer vacuoles and vesicles.\")\n\n  Line 20052: # Class: obo:CL_0002574 (stromal cell of pancreas)\n\n  Line 20054: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002574 \"A stromal cell of the pancreas.\")\n\n  Line 20057: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002574 \"stromal cell of pancreas\")\n\n  Line 20500: # Class: obo:CL_0002622 (prostate stromal cell)\n\n  Line 20502: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002622 \"A stromal cell of the prostate.\")\n\n  Line 20506: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002622 \"prostate stromal cell\")\n\n  Line 23530: # Class: obo:CL_0009021 (stromal cell of lamina propria of large intestine)\n\n  Line 23532: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009021 \"A stromal cell found in the lamina propria of the large intestine.\")\n\n  Line 23535: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009021 \"stromal cell of lamina propria of large intestine\")\n\n  Line 23538: # Class: obo:CL_0009022 (stromal cell of lamina propria of small intestine)\n\n  Line 23540: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009022 \"A stromal cell found in the lamina propria of the small intestine.\")\n\n  Line 23543: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009022 \"stromal cell of lamina propria of small intestine\")\n\n  Line 23681: # Class: obo:CL_0009035 (stromal cell of lamina propria of vermiform appendix)\n\n  Line 23683: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009035 \"A stromal cell found in the lamina propria of the vermiform appendix.\")\n\n  Line 23685: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009035 \"stromal cell of appendix lamina propria\")\n\n  Line 23686: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009035 \"stromal cell of lamina propria of appendix vermiformis\")\n\n  Line 23688: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009035 \"stromal cell of lamina propria of vermiform appendix\")\n\n  Line 23733: # Class: obo:CL_0009040 (stromal cell of lamina propria of colon)\n\n  Line 23735: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009040 \"A stromal cell found in the lamina propria of the colon.\")\n\n  Line 23737: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009040 \"stromal cell of colon lamina propria\")\n\n  Line 23739: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009040 \"stromal cell of lamina propria of colon\")\n\n  Line 23864: # Class: obo:CL_0009053 (stromal cell of anorectum lamina propria)\n\n  Line 23866: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009053 \"A stromal cell found in the lamina propria of the anorectum.\")\n\n  Line 23869: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009053 \"stromal cell of anorectum lamina propria\")\n\n  Line 24543: # Class: obo:CL_0010001 (stromal cell of bone marrow)\n\n  Line 24545: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0010001 \"A stromal cell that is part_of a bone marrow.\")\n\n  Line 24547: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0010001 \"bone marrow stromal cell\")\n\n  Line 24548: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0010001 \"stromal cell of bone marrow\")\n\n  Line 25456: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31324739\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33707780\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34046914\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34497389\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020000 \"A mesenchymal stromal cell found in the gut during development, and interacts with lymphoid tissue inducer (LTi) cells to drive secondary lymphoid organ formation (Prados et al., 2021). It expresses LTβR, PDGFRα, and VCAM, and upon activation secretes chemokines(e.g. CXCL13) and cytokines to organise lymphoid tissue architecture and recruit immune cells in both mice and humans (Denton el al., 2019; Elmentaite et al., 2021). As a multipotent progenitor, an mLTo cell differentiates into adult stromal subsets, including fibroblastic reticular cells (FRCs) (Prados et al., 2021), and its descendants persist in the adult gut-associated lymphoid tissues to maintain immune homeostasis(Denton el al., 2019; Lütge et al., 2021).\")\n\n  Line 25637: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34280086\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2023.12.07.570646\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020016 \"A tissue-specific stem cell with long-term self-renewal capacity that is restricted to generating bone, cartilage, and stromal cell lineages. This cell is primarily located in the growth plate (resting zone), periosteum, and subchondral bone regions, and is marked by high clonogenicity and robust multipotent differentiation potential in both osteogenic and chondrogenic lineages. Distinctively, ocSSC lacks adipogenic capacity, distinguishing it from other mesenchymal stem cell populations.\")\n\n  Line 26400: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28028137\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1000308 \"A stromal cell that is part of the outer adventitial layer of the ureter. This cell type is marked by expression of periostin (POSTN) in mice, and it is derived from Foxd1+ mesenchymal progenitors around embryonic day 12.5. The adventitial fibrocyte initiates differentiation earlier than smooth muscle cells and becomes terminally differentiated by E16.5-18.5 in mice, exhibiting low proliferative capacity in adulthood.\")\n\n  Line 28064: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23486523\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27262400\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35703942\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1000693 \"A stromal cell that infiltrates and resides in the kidney interstitium following injury, characterized by the co-expression of CD45 with mesenchymal markers including α-SMA, and collagen I in humans (Kim et al., 2023). This cell originates from circulating monocyte-derived fibrocytes. It produces extracellular matrix components, contributing to renal fibrosis by potentially differentiating into myofibroblasts upon infiltration into injured kidneys (Sun et al., 2016). Migration into the kidney is dependent on chemokine receptor signaling, particularly CCR2 in mice (Reich et al., 2013).\")\n\n  Line 29317: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"BTO:0002770\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"NCIT:C32429\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30013421\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30429548\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wiki:Decidual_cells&oldid=937509751\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wiki:Decidualization&oldid=908981933\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_2000002 \"A specialized, enlarged, connective tissue cell of the decidua with enlarged nucleus, dense membrane‐bound secretory granules and cytoplasmic accumulation of glycogen and lipid droplets. These cells develop by the transformation of endometrial stromal cells during decidualization.\")\n\n  Line 29323: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"BTO:0005756\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11719592\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_2000002 \"decidual stromal cell\")\n\n  Line 29324: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31907034\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_2000002 \"decidualized endometrial stromal cell\")\n\n  Line 29877: # Class: obo:CL_2000061 (placental amniotic mesenchymal stromal cell)\n\n  Line 29884: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_2000061 \"placental amniotic mesenchymal stromal cell\")\n\n  Line 31829: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4028006 \"type-2 associated stromal cell\")\n\n  Line 31878: # Class: obo:CL_4030001 (stromal cell of thymus)\n\n  Line 31880: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41467-020-20082-7\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030001 \"A stromal cell that is part of the thymus.\")\n\n  Line 31882: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030001 \"thymic stromal cell\")\n\n  Line 31883: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030001 \"stromal cell of thymus\")\n\n  Line 34454: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20628033\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31320652\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36205477\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052010 \"A stromal cell that serves as a precursor to the theca cell layers in the ovary growing follicles. This cell is present in the early stages of follicular growth, particularly in smaller follicles. Unlike mature theca cell, a pre-theca cell is initially non-steroidogenic and lacks luteinizing hormone receptors.\")\n\n  Line 34814: # Class: obo:CL_4052045 (steroidogenic stromal cell of ovary)\n\n  Line 34816: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36205477\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1101/2024.12.15.628550\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052045 \"A stromal cell that is part of the ovarian stroma, characterized by its ability to synthesize steroid hormones.\")\n\n  Line 34819: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36205477\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4052045 \"steroidogenic interstitial stromal cell\")\n\n  Line 34820: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36205477\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4052045 \"steroidogenic stromal cell\")\n\n  Line 34822: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052045 \"steroidogenic stromal cell of ovary\")\n","metadata":{"matches":70,"truncated":false},"title":"Fasciacyte|fasciacyte|deep fascia|fascia lata|mesenchymal stromal cell|stromal cell","time":{"start":1778979828335,"end":1778979828510}},"id":"prt_e3375f269001vg1FK76PKd4O4y","sessionID":"ses_1cc8a5276ffe1gnevDwHegZIZv","messageID":"msg_e3375cce7001yJ2I4vkHK27Nc1"}}
