science, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\") , [Caterina Fede](/?term=Fede+C&cauthor_id=29575206)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\") , [Veronica Macchi](/?term=Macchi+V&cauthor_id=29575206)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\") , [Andrea Porzionato](/?term=Porzionato+A&cauthor_id=29575206)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\") , [Lucia Petrelli](/?term=Petrelli+L&cauthor_id=29575206)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\") , [Carlo Biz](/?term=Biz+C&cauthor_id=29575206)  [2](#full-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Surgery, Oncology and Gastroenterology DiSCOG, Orthopedic Clinic, University of Padova, via Giustiniani 2, Padova, 35121, Italy.\") , [Robert Stern](/?term=Stern+R&cauthor_id=29575206)  [3](#full-view-affiliation-3 \"Division of Basic Biomedical Sciences, Touro College of Osteopathic Medicine, 230 West-125th Street, New York, New York, 10027.\") , [Raffaele De Caro](/?term=De+Caro+R&cauthor_id=29575206)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\")\n\nAffiliations Expand\n\n### Affiliations\n\n-   1 Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\n-   2 Department of Surgery, Oncology and Gastroenterology DiSCOG, Orthopedic Clinic, University of Padova, via Giustiniani 2, Padova, 35121, Italy.\n-   3 Division of Basic Biomedical Sciences, Touro College of Osteopathic Medicine, 230 West-125th Street, New York, New York, 10027.\n\n-   PMID: **29575206**\n-   DOI: [10.1002/ca.23072](https://doi.org/10.1002/ca.23072)\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\n# The fasciacytes: A new cell devoted to fascial gliding regulation\n\nCarla Stecco et al. Clin Anat. 2018 Jul.\n\nShow details\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat Abstract PubMed PMID\n\nClin Anat\n\nActions\n\n-   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Clin+Anat%22%5Bjour%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n-   [Search in NLM Catalog](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/nlmcatalog?term=%22Clin+Anat%22%5BTitle+Abbreviation%5D)\n-   [Add to Search](#)\n\n. 2018 Jul;31(5):667-676.\n\ndoi: 10.1002/ca.23072. Epub 2018 Apr 14.\n\n### Authors\n\n[Carla Stecco](/?term=Stecco+C&cauthor_id=29575206)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\") , [Caterina Fede](/?term=Fede+C&cauthor_id=29575206)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\") , [Veronica Macchi](/?term=Macchi+V&cauthor_id=29575206)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\") , [Andrea Porzionato](/?term=Porzionato+A&cauthor_id=29575206)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\") , [Lucia Petrelli](/?term=Petrelli+L&cauthor_id=29575206)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\") , [Carlo Biz](/?term=Biz+C&cauthor_id=29575206)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Surgery, Oncology and Gastroenterology DiSCOG, Orthopedic Clinic, University of Padova, via Giustiniani 2, Padova, 35121, Italy.\") , [Robert Stern](/?term=Stern+R&cauthor_id=29575206)  [3](#short-view-affiliation-3 \"Division of Basic Biomedical Sciences, Touro College of Osteopathic Medicine, 230 West-125th Street, New York, New York, 10027.\") , [Raffaele De Caro](/?term=De+Caro+R&cauthor_id=29575206)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\")\n\n### Affiliations\n\n-   1 Department of Neuroscience, University of Padova, via Gabelli 65, Padova, 35121, Italy.\n-   2 Department of Surgery, Oncology and Gastroenterology DiSCOG, Orthopedic Clinic, University of Padova, via Giustiniani 2, Padova, 35121, Italy.\n-   3 Division of Basic Biomedical Sciences, Touro College of Osteopathic Medicine, 230 West-125th Street, New York, New York, 10027.\n\n-   PMID: **29575206**\n-   DOI: [10.1002/ca.23072](https://doi.org/10.1002/ca.23072)\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nFull text links Cite\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat AbstractPubMedPMID\n\n## Abstract\n\nHyaluronan occurs between deep fascia and muscle, facilitating gliding between these two structures, and also within the loose connective tissue of the fascia, guaranteeing the smooth sliding of adjacent fibrous fascial layers. It also promotes the functions of the deep fascia. In this study a new class of cells in fasciae is identified, which we have termed fasciacytes, devoted to producing the hyaluronan-rich extracellular matrix. Synthesis of the hyaluronan-rich matrix by these new cells was demonstrated by Alcian Blue staining, anti-HABP (hyaluronic acid binding protein) immunohistochemistry, and transmission electron microscopy. Expression of HAS2 (hyaluronan synthase 2) mRNA by these cells was detected and quantified using real time RT-PCR. This new cell type has some features similar to fibroblasts: they are positive for the fibroblast marker vimentin and negative for CD68, a marker for the monocyte-macrophage lineage. However, they have morphological features distinct from classical fibroblasts and they express the marker for chondroid metaplasia, S-100A4. The authors suggest that these cells represent a new cell type devoted to the production of hyaluronan. Since hyaluronan is essential for fascial gliding, regulation of these cells could affect the functions of fasciae so they could be implicated in myofascial pain. Clin. Anat. 31:667-676, 2018. © 2018 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.\n\n**Keywords:** extracellular matrix; fascia; fasciacytes; hyaluronan.\n\n© 2018 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.\n\n[PubMed Disclaimer](/disclaimer/)\n\n## MeSH terms\n\n-   Aged\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Aged%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Aged)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Aged, 80 and over\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Aged%2C+80+and+over%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Aged%2C+80+and+over)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Fascia Lata / cytology\\*\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Fascia+Lata%2Fcytology%22%5BMAJR%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Fascia+Lata)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Fascia Lata / metabolism\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Fascia+Lata%2Fmetabolism%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Fascia+Lata)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Female\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Female%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Female)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Fibroblasts / ultrastructure\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Fibroblasts%2Fultrastructure%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Fibroblasts)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Humans\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Humans%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Humans)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Hyaluronic Acid